<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

`<<~ kau #frag Name props>>` places a device instance into the carrier. kau = "to place upon, set down with intention" (Hawaiian).

Each kau placement creates a device instance with:
* ''Instance URI'': `carrierUri#fragment` (explicit `#frag` required; auto-UUID deferred to action tiddler when Keyhive WASM lands)
* ''Own execution context'': `currentTiddler` set to instance URI before transcluding the kumu def
* ''Persistent addressability'': instance URI becomes UCAN resource for per-instance capability grants (Keyhive deferred)

''The widget reads the argument RUN, not the slots.'' Its shape runs positional-by-PREFIX rather than positional-by-arity — a placement carries a fragment the invocation form omits — so `args` parse decides: the first token opening with `#` reads as the fragment, and the remainder reads as name plus props.

Invocation form: `<<~ kau Name>>` — no fragment; transcludes the kumu definition in the caller's context.

Resolves the kumu definition via `[all[tiddlers+shadows]tag[lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/kumu]field:kumu-name<_kau-name>first[]else[]]`.
Placement renders `<div class="lar-kau lar-kau-place" data-uri="…">`.
Invocation renders `<div class="lar-kau lar-kau-invoke">`.
An unresolved device shows `<span class="lar-kau-hole">`.

!!! Render surface

`\widget ~kau(p1:"" p2:"" p3:"" args:"")` lives in `packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/sigil-kau.tid`. The template cascade takes the first tiddler tagged `lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/kau-template` and falls back to `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/templates/kau/html`. That template branches on the fragment: a non-empty `kau-frag` renders the placement div carrying `data-uri`, `data-kau-name` and, where present, `data-kau-props`; an empty one renders the invocation div.

Companion procedures: `~kahea~kau` (live transclusion of the kau child-slot), `~aka~kau` (frozen projection through the aka template cascade).

!!! Keyhive stubs — deferred

Per-instance capability hooks and UUID write-back surface as explicit TW5 action tiddlers when Keyhive WASM lands. The widget itself holds no JS module hooks.

<<~/ahu>>

